  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "An arch of a bridge is semi-elliptical with major axis horizontal. If the length the base is 9 meter and the highest part of the bridge is 3 meter from the horizontal; the best approximation of the height of the arch. 2 meter from the centre of the base is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GDvbY",
      "text": "$11 / 4 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bzApR",
      "text": "$8 / 3 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "1gxkH",
      "text": "$7 / 2 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9YRIH",
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/2hq8a_AlD6WCdS2CUiDQ8R63IEfVVdLzZaSb81arPZ0.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nThe equation of the ellipse is\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\frac{x^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)^{2}}+\\frac{y^{2}}{9}=1\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nWhere centre is assumed as origin and base as $x$ -axis. Put $x=2,$ we get\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\frac{16}{81}+\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^{2}}{9}=1 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{y}=\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}{3} \\approx \\frac{8}{3} \\mathrm{~m}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n(approximately)",
    "image": null
  },
